  "In the competitive landscape of the primary inbox, visual identity and trust verification directly dictate open rates. The pinnacle of modern email authentication is BIMI: Brand Indicators for Message Identification. BIMI is an open technical specification that enables verified organizations to display their official corporate trademark logo directly adjacent to inbound messages in the email client UI—across Apple Mail, Gmail, and Yahoo Mail. Implementing BIMI requires meeting strict cryptographic prerequisites. First, the sending domain must have DMARC fully enforced at either 'p=quarantine' (with pct=100) or 'p=reject'. A domain running 'p=none' is strictly ineligible for BIMI. Second, the corporate logo must be converted into a standardized, cryptographically formatted SVG Tiny P/S (Portable/Secure) vector graphic. Third, to display logos in Gmail, Google requires a Verified Mark Certificate (VMC).",
