        "why": "RRF sums the reciprocal ranks across models (1/(k+r_lex) + 1/(k+r_dense)); documents present near the top of both lists accumulate larger combined scores than documents present in only one list.",
        "explanation": "RRF sums the reciprocal ranks across models (1/(k+r_lex) + 1/(k+r_dense)); documents present near the top of both lists accumulate larger combined scores than documents present in only one list."
